==Characteristics==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|Fire Chuchu}}
Fire Chuchus are flaming [[Chuchu]]s that appear in hot places, such as the [[Eldin (Region)|Eldin]] [[Region]].<ref name="BotW Hyrule Compendium 2"/> [[Fire Wizzrobe]]s and [[Meteo Wizzrobe]]s are also capable of summoning them.<ref name="BotW Hyrule Compendium 3"/> They leave trails of [[Fire]] behind them as they move, igniting flammable materials such as [[Grass]]. Fire Chuchus come in three different sizes, with their strength correlating to how large they are.<ref name="BotW Hyrule Compendium 2"/>

Fire Chuchus attack by dashing forward and emitting a blast of Fire around them.<ref name="CaC 150"/> If hit by their attack, [[Link]] will be temporarily set on Fire, but this can be avoided by wearing the full [[Flamebreaker Set|Fireproof Armor]] for the [[Fireproof]] [[Set Bonus]]. After attacking, Fire Chuchus temporarily lose their fiery coating and become a darker color, leaving them vulnerable. If they are defeated while on Fire, they will explode with a fiery blast. As a result, the [[Hyrule Compendium]] suggests fighting them at a distance by utilizing [[Spear]]s or shooting [[Arrow]]s.<ref name="BotW Hyrule Compendium 2"/> Fire Chuchus drop [[Red Chuchu Jelly]] after being defeated.

